ical Gulf-of-Alaska coastal width (regional summary)","phase_kind":"regional_scalar_summary","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"regional_scalar_context":{"audit_file":"research/alaska-coastal-gulf-jarosz-2017-regional-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"308e05e7c1c8122aaee0b917b85822b1162b8b25021aa0f77387eca11714843b","boundary_coordinates_supplied":false,"bathymetry_is_measurement_layer":false},"remaining_gates":["Review original width definitions behind the introductory literature synthesis.","Obtain paired boundaries and compatible repeated sections before seasonal dimension ranges.","Independent scientific and canonical admission review."],"source_quality_note":"Typical-width literature statement, not a measured winter width from the article experiment. Original contributing definitions remain unreviewed."},{"id":"mindanao-schonau-2015-mean-surface-offshore-extent","current_id":"mindanao-current","name":"Mindanao Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_mean_surface_offshore_extent_range","width_metric":"author_reported_mean_surface_equatorward_offshore_extent","approximate_width_km":null,"width_range_km":[250,300],"range_kind":"author_reported_approximate_offshore_extent_of_mean_surface_flow","range_interpretation":"Approximate range in the author’s prose description of one averaged surface section; not uncertainty, seasonal extrema or a paired-boundary full width.","geographic_scope":"Oblique mean line from 8.16 N, 126.61 E to 8.77 N, 130 E off Mindanao. Profiles within 80 km were projected and objectively mapped; not an along-current envelope.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Oblique mean line; reported offshore distance retained without converting it to paired cross-flow edges.","layer":"Surface expression of averaged absolute geostrophic equatorward flow. The 0–1000 m glider velocity reference is not a fixed measurement layer for this extent.","fixe