erval":false,"source_date_discrepancy":"p.35 describes intended repeated sections June 2009–January 2014; p.36 reports deployments June 2009–July 2014. Neither supplies exact profiles entering Figure 2.","boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"velocity_threshold_m_s":null,"offshore_secondary_core_may_be_eddy":true,"secondary_core_location_is_current_width":false,"transport_integration_limit_is_current_width":false,"audit_file":"research/mindanao-schonau-2015-mean-offshore-extent-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"6d5ff66c68d353d6f34bd3440945327baca6578d130a2014bd439c1af37f376d"}},{"id":"agulhas-return-boebel-2003-adcp-a","current_id":"agulhas-return","name":"Agulhas Return Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_multilayer_ADCP_threshold_width","width_metric":"median_across_ADCP_depth_bins_of_flow_normal_half_maximum_isotach_distance","approximate_width_km":48,"reported_total_error_km":14,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"Source ± total error estimate is stored separately; no confidence level or seasonal range supplied. Projection error is already a component of total error.","geographic_scope":"Near 39 S, 22 E; source body differs from preliminary poster 23 E. Local Seward Johnson cruise crossing, not the full current envelope.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Flow-normal projection for each depth bin; source reports a median across bin widths.","layer":"Near-surface and upper-ocean ADCP bins; deepest reported bin 325–375 m, nominal center 350 m. Width is a median across bins, not a fixed-depth surface width or 0–1000 m width.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"time_convention":"1997 cruise context only; exact dates of this crossing not extracted. Figure 3a MODAS SSH date 1997-08-23 is contextual imagery; source says cruise ends 10 days later. Exact dates of the four crossings are not extracted. Crossings b2 and c approximately one day apart.","boundary_rule":"Distance between half-maximum vel