ription":"Slightly stronger than March; maximum not transcribed","whole_voyage_context":{"start":"1997-12-01","end":"1997-12-09","is_exact_section_support":false}}]},"protocol_file":"plans/zeehan-width-source-separation-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"fadd4e4eff23f524ccdd16aaa6e1f906bb46c9b2bc23dca8cc082c7865f82411","display_caption":"Approximate 40 km historical slope-current width near western Bass Strait, attributed to Baines et al. (1983). Numerical uncertainty and paired edges unknown; not a 1997 Strahan section width.","display_method_note":"Separate 1997 Strahan evidence: December is described as narrower and slightly stronger than March. Neither section has a numerical width here. Two occupations do not establish annual extrema or a monthly climatology; 300 m ADCP coverage is not the historical width layer.","audit_file":"research/zeehan-cresswell-2000-width-section-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"83b7c97d7d30ff2b2044bfc12316d99806b3005da5709afbf385a7f485c1f0c5"}},{"id":"tsushima-matsuyama-1990-nearshore-modal-width","current_id":"tsushima","name":"Tsushima Current","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_campaign_modal_decay_estimate","width_metric":"coast_to_modal_decay_threshold_distance","approximate_width_km":22,"width_range_km":null,"range_kind":"reported_modal_estimate_with_unresolved_arithmetic_discrepancy","range_interpretation":"Reported 22 km; summary approximately 20 km and recalculation 23.0769 km describe the same estimate. They do not define a measured range or numerical uncertainty.","geographic_scope":"Nearshore branch over the continental shelf off the San’in coast, Japan Sea; not the entire Tsushima Current system.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Offshore y direction approximately northward from the east–west coast in the source model; paired edge coordinates unresolved.","layer":"First baroclinic mode under summer density stratification; eastward above the seasonal thermocline and westward below. No fixed width slab extracted.","time_convention":"Finite July–August 1980 campaign. Modal coefficient from the 8 August hydrographic profile; station and current-average durations differ. No homogeneous width occupation interval or recurring seasonal calendar assigned.","boundary_rule":"Offshore modal amplitude exp(-gamma_1*y), relative to its coastal value; adopted exp(-3) decay criterion (approximately 5%). Printed gamma_1=1.3e-4 m^-1.","source_url":"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/kaiyou1942/46/4/46_4_156/_pdf","source_citation":"Matsuyama, M. (1990), The Structure of the Nearshore Branch of the Tsushima Current on the Shelf off the San’in Coast in Summer, Journal of the Oceanographical Society of Japan 46(4):156–166, doi:10.1007/BF02125576.","source_locator":"Printed p165 / PDF page 10, Discussion decay equation and Summary(1); eigenvalue and fit method p161 / PDF page 6; station dates p158 and common average p159; separate Fig10 p164.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_campaign_modal_diagnosis","extraction_method":"Manual original equation and context transcription with visual verification; independently calculate printed arithmetic, without digitizing current boundaries.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"1980 coastal-branch modal estimate","phase_kind":"campaign_modal_decay_width","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Reported 22 km disagrees with 3/(1.3e-4) m = 23.0769 km; cause unresolved. Approximately 20 km is a summary of the same estimate. Fig10 caption 134°E conflicts with Discussion 132°E; the climatological section is separate support. Printed Eq8 plus sign is inconsistent with the stated exponential solution for real positive gamma; no correction inferred.","remaining_gates":["Resolve source differential-equation sign and arithmetic discrepancies; independent scientific admission.","Extract geographically located compatible boundaries and uncertainty.","Acquire repeat occupations before seasonal ranges or playback."],"modal_decay_context":{"normalized_amplitude_equation":"Y(y)/Y(0)=exp(-gamma_1*y)","coastal_reference_amplitude":1,"printed_gamma_per_m":0.00013,"edge_exponent":3,"edge_relative_amplitude":0.049787068367863944,"source_rounded_relative_amplitude":0.05,"source_reported_width_km":22,"source_summary_width_km_approx":20,"recalculated_width_km":23.076923076923077,"arithmetic_discrepancy_unresolved":true,"summary_is_independent_measurement":false,"discrepancy_is_uncertainty_interval":false,"coefficient_method":"Separation constant of density-profile eigenvalue problem (Eq7 with boundary conditions); least-squares fits current data to computed mode shapes, not an offshore velocity-coefficient fit.","model_assumptions":["Hydrostatic and Boussinesq approximations","Flat bottom and rigid lid","Zero initial potential vorticity; coast-relative exponential offshore mode"],"fitted_current_modes":["barotropic","first_baroclinic"],"campaign_context":{"start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-25","is_homogeneous_width_observation_period":false},"station_support":[{"station":"A","start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-25","source_reported_days":31},{"station":"B","start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-25","source_reported_days":31},{"station":"C","start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-14","source_reported_days":19},{"station":"D","start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-14","source_reported_days":19},{"station":"E","start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-14","source_reported_days":19}],"common_current_mean_period":{"start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-14","source_locator":"Printed p159, section4: common period for five-station time averages."},"station_B_modal_mean_period":{"start":"1980-07-26","end":"1980-08-25","source_locator":"Printed p162, Figure8 discussion: entire B record."},"hydrographic_profile_support":{"station":"H","date":"1980-08-08","latitude_degrees_north":36.15,"longitude_degrees_east":134.13333333333333,"role":"Density profile input for computed vertical modes; not a current edge."},"instrument_context":{"surface_offset_m":10,"bottom_offset_m":10,"sampling_interval_minutes":10,"is_fixed_width_layer":false},"shelf_context":{"coast_to_200m_isobath_km":[15,20],"is_width_range":false},"separate_hydrographic_climatology":{"start_year":1964,"end_year":1985,"calendar_months":[7,8,9],"caption_longitude_degrees_east":134,"discussion_longitude_degrees_east":132,"longitude_conflict":true,"is_1980_width_support":false},"boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"summer_campaign_is_recurring_calendar":false,"display_caption":"Coastal branch · reported modal width 22 km (summer 1980). Diagram illustrates the published exponential expression; its differential-equation sign remains unresolved. No mapped edge or seasonal range.","display_method_note":"The source adopts roughly 5% of coastal amplitude as the edge. Its printed coefficient gives 23.1 km; the paper reports 22 km and summarizes about 20 km. Arithmetic discrepancy unresolved; numerical uncertainty unknown.","offshore_equation_consistency":{"source_locator":"Printed p161 / PDF page 6, Eq8 and following solution statement; original visually verified.","printed_equation":"d2Y_n/dy2+gamma_n^2*Y_n=0","stated_solution":"Y_n~exp(-gamma_n*y)","finding_class":"editorial_mathematical_consistency_check_not_author_correction","inconsistent_for_real_positive_gamma":true,"sign_resolution":null,"diagram_validates_printed_differential_equation":false},"audit_file":"research/tsushima-matsuyama-1990-modal-width-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"587cccbd45b3673137523241a2bbab07f3ee681e8f5549a7b44f0ae6ced90fb6"}},{"id":"west-australian-glenn-2008-offshore-breadth-constraint","current_id":"west-australian","name":"West Australian Curr