y_caption":"C1, 24-28 May 2017: inflow identified as part of EAC was confined to roughly the first 10 km offshore. This is a local coastal extent, with exact width occupation day unresolved.","display_method_note":"ADCP sampled 10-70 m; plotted surface arrows represent 10 m. The 20 km upwelling/pycnocline extent is a different object. C2 supplies no numeric EAC width, so no annual or seasonal range is inferred.","quality_note":"Author conference abstract and figure inspected; one local reported extent, no raw ADCP data or thresholded boundary pair. Exact width day and width at each sampled depth not independently resolved.","audit_file":"research/east-adriatic-pasaric-2019-inflow-extent-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"d5e5d83fb84cd1243a5a4dd44b4dd3104ed2dd6c61276d29146b2bfda60e4993","audit_pointer":"/measurements/0"}},{"id":"pacific-secc-rotschi-1972-170e-width-range","current_id":"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","name":"Pacific South Equatorial Countercurrent","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","phase_kind":"regional_summary","width_metric":"author_reported_geostrophic_current_width_range","width_metric_label":"historical local geostrophic width range","approximate_width_km":null,"width_range_km":[300,900],"range_kind":"reported_historical_cruise_width_span","range_interpretation":"Historical local source range across cruise-study context. Endpoint occupations, statistical uncertainty and annual extrema unresolved; no midpoint selected.","geographic_scope":"170 E meridional sections, geostrophic SECC near 10 S. Excludes South Tropical Countercurrent south of 15 S and the subsurface/equatorial Cromwell extensions.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Meridional source sections; no independently reconstructed edges or flow-normal correction.","layer":"Author geostrophic-current envelope with broad vertical support; exact width depth and reference level unresolved. Speeds above 10 cm/s generally within upper 300 m is a separate statement, not a 0–300 m width slab.","time_convention":"November 1965–May 1968 Bora/Cyclone cruise-study context. No individual dates assigned to width range endpoints; not seasonal climatology or annual extrema.","boundary_rule":"Author-reported geostrophic current width; exact velocity cutoff, paired lateral coordinates and reference level not specified in the inspected descriptor. Direct equatorial meters referenced to 500 m are a different method.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/divers20-05/010028590.pdf#page=13","source_citation":"Rotschi, H., Hisard, Ph. and Jarrige, F. (1972), The Water Masses of the Western Pacific at 170 E, between 20 S and 4 N, Survey Paper No. 15, Horace Lamb Centre / ORSTOM, advanced English adaptation. Preface dated 10 May 1972.","source_locator":"Current discussion printed p10 / PDF13; cruise context printed pp3–4 / PDF6–7; method distinction printed p6 / PDF9; title/preface PDF1–2.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-13","source_evidence_kind":"primary_historical_geostrophic_section_width_summary","extraction_method":"Range transcribed from visually reviewed original prose. No source figure or velocity boundaries digitized.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Historical Pacific SECC width range at 170 E","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"time_precision":"multicruise_context_width_endpoint_dates_unresolved","source_quality_note":"Complete original report inspected. Repeated historical geostrophic sections support an author width range; raw boundary calculations and endpoint occupations were not recovered.","remaining_gates":["Resolve geostrophic reference level, width layer and paired boundary criterion before physical comparison.","Recover range endpoint occupations and compatible repeated sections before annual or seasonal dimensions."],"original_regional_context":{"description_kind":"historical_geostrophic_cruise_range","source_reported_core_latitude_neighborhood_south":10,"source_section_longitude_east":170,"source_quoted_current_name":"South Equatorial Countercurrent","source_width_range_km":[300,900],"width_range_is_annual":false,"range_endpoints_assigned_to_cruises":false,"paired_velocity_boundaries_extracted":false,"source_figures_digitized":false,"uniform_300m_width_layer_admitted":false,"direct_meter_500m_reference_transferred":false,"geostrophic_reference_level_resolved":false,"study_period_months":["1965-11","1968-05"],"survey_cruise_count":11,"evidence_class":"primary_historical_geostrophic_section_width_summary","time_precision":"multicruise_context_width_endpoint_dates_unresolved","display_title":"Historical Pacific SECC width range at 170 E","display_aria_label":"Pacific SECC near 10 S at 170 E: source-reported historical 300 to 900 km width range. No midpoint, annual extrema, paired mapped boundaries or numerical uncertainty supplied.","display_caption":"Near 10 S at 170 E: 300–900 km geostrophic-current width description from the 1965–1968 cruise study. The range endpoints are not assigned to individual cruise dates; no midpoint or annual range inferred.","display_method_note":"This SECC is distinct from the deeper equatorial/subsurface extensions and the South Tropical Countercurrent south of 15 S. Width layer, geostrophic reference level and paired boundary criterion remain unresolved. The upper-300 m speed statement and direct current-meter 500 m reference are separate descriptors.","quality_note":"Complete original report inspected. Repeated historical geostrophic sections support an author width range; raw boundary calculations and endpoint occupations were not recovered.","source_pdf_sha256":"f2d8d1c8ba9655146319829b942278a13ac792b4a634e6d547a2cd17bc6b24fe","protocol_file":"plans/pac