h no paired edge coordinates extracted.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Meridional western WOA-Box section; no exact flow-normal correction inferred.","layer":"Depth-varying inverse-model section. Source reports maximum core depth about 790 m in spring and 1100 m in autumn; these are source-reported vertical context, not fixed depth layers at which these widths were measured.","time_convention":"WOA09 mixed historical climatologies in a regional inverse model; source quarter WOA09 spring climatology (April-June). Not an individual occupation or dated current footprint.","boundary_rule":"Author defines the core using velocities greater than 2 cm/s. No full-current envelope or universal half-peak threshold inferred.","source_url":"https://nora.nerc.ac.uk/id/eprint/521101/1/1-s2.0-S0079661113002437-main.pdf","source_citation":"Carracedo, Gilcoto, Mercier and Perez (2014), Seasonal dynamics in the Azores-Gibraltar Strait region: A climatologically-based study, Progress in Oceanography 122, 116-130, doi:10.1016/j.pocean.2013.12.005.","source_locator":"Section 3.1.1.1, printed page 122 / PDF page 7; methods section 2.1, printed page 118 / PDF page 3.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-14","source_evidence_kind":"published_inverse_model_climatological_core_summary","extraction_method":"Author-reported values transcribed from original prose; no contour digitization or model reproduction.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"observed_period":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"remaining_gates":["Recover original model fields and paired boundaries before geometry or scientific reproduction.","Width error and whole-current dimensions remain unknown.","Independent scientific and canonical admission."],"calendar_source_locator":"World Ocean Atlas 2009 Volume 1, Introduction, printed page 1 / PDF page 13","calend