ed geographic width limits supplied.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Cross-shelf/slope section context; no exact paired width endpoints or flow-normal orientation diagnosed by OSW.","layer":"Detided LADCP horizontal-current context at 100 m (paragraph 5 and Figure 1). Surface-intensified jet; no uniform vertical width slab inferred. 3000 m isobath describes bottom topography.","time_convention":"One observed section on 23 February 2009; January 31 is separate. Neither the 2010 publication date nor the M6 2017–2021 record dates this jet.","boundary_rule":"Author reports jet narrower than 28 km. Velocity cutoff and paired edges unresolved; peak 28 cm/s and broader-flow speed about 10 cm/s are not boundary thresholds.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2010GL043603","source_citation":"Chavanne, C.P., K.J. Heywood, K.W. Nicholls and I. Fer (2010), Observations of the Antarctic Slope Undercurrent in the southeastern Weddell Sea, Geophysical Research Letters 37, L13601, doi:10.1029/2010GL043603.","source_locator":"Primary publisher indexed text: section 2 Observations paragraph 5; processing paragraph 4; Figure 1/2 captions establish section dates and 100 m horizontal-current context.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-14","source_evidence_kind":"published_primary_indexed_dated_jet_width_constraint","extraction_method":"Reported qualifier, reference scale and date transcribed from primary publisher indexed body/captions; original PDF/pixels and fields not acquired or digitized.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_label":"Riiser-Larsenisen narrow surface jet (23 February 2009)","phase_kind":"dated_width_constraint","observed_period":{"start":"2009-02-23","end":"2009-02-23"},"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"source_quality_note":"Primary publisher indexed passages/captions reviewed. Original PDF, figure pixels, fields and paired width edges unavailable. Width constraint describes a narrow jet within broader flow, not complete ASC width.","remaining_gates":["Acquire original paper/figures and paired width boundary method.","Recover compatible repeated sections before seasonal widths or annual extrema.","Independent scientific admission."],"original_regional_context":{"description_kind":"indexed_dated_jet_width_constraint","full_original_inspected":false,"figure_pixels_inspected":false,"paired_edges_extracted":false,"zero_to_reference_is_width_range":false,"reference_scale_is_point_width":false,"is_annual_range":false,"jet_width_is_broader_flow_width":false,"speed_context_is_width_cutoff":false,"bathy_is_width_layer":false,"point_depth_context_m":100,"peak_speed_cm_s":28,"background_speed_cm_s_approx":10,"bottom_isobath_m":3000,"station_ids":[138,139,140,141,142,143,144],"sampling_date":"2009-02-23","processing_context":"LADCP LDEO IX.5; least-squares M2 tidal removal from depth-averaged currents; source-reported, not reproduced by OSW.","protocol_file":"plans/antarctic-slope-chavanne-2010-width-constraint-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"ffa1b604f782ec1b0b696f5c5a2e9ad733cd7ba01be6af2bad3d714c4f526d85","display_aria_label":"Antarctic Slope Current narrow jet: source reports less than 28 km on 23 February 2009, in 100 m detided LADCP context. No point width, lower bound, zero-to-28 interval, confidence guarantee or full-current envelope.","display_caption":"Source reports a narrow southwestward jet <28 km on 23 February 2009, within broader slower southwestward flow. Representative width, lower bound and numeric uncertainty remain unknown.","display_method_note":"Primary publisher indexed text/captions reviewed; original PDF and figure pixels unavailable. 100 m is the horizontal-current context; 3000 m is bottom topography. Peak 28 cm/s and background about 10 cm/s are not width 