; local branch support, not whole-route dimensions.","layer":"Near-barotropic eastern branch; no fixed width measurement depth.","boundary_rule":"No paired coordinates or velocity cutoff supplied by the abstract width statement.","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"section_geometry":null,"whole_current_representative":false,"rank_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0967063700000388","source_citation":"Orvik, K. A., Skagseth, O. and Mork, M. (2001), Atlantic inflow to the Nordic Seas: current structure and volume fluxes from moored current meters, VM-ADCP and SeaSoar-CTD observations, 1995-1999, Deep-Sea Research I 48, 937-957, doi:10.1016/S0967-0637(00)00038-8.","source_locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract, eastern and western branch width statements.","source_access":"Publisher-indexed abstract inspected. Full original 2001 article and figures remain unreviewed.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","sampling_context":{"mooring_context_months":{"start":"1995-04","end":"1999-02"},"mooring_context_is_width_sampling_interval":false,"mooring_bathymetry_m":[490,990],"bathymetry_is_width_layer":false,"reported_jet_depth_m":null,"jet_depth_is_width_layer":false},"temporal_interpretation":"Mooring program dates are context, not a dated width series. No annual or seasonal range established.","unit":"km","full_width_inference_eligible":false,"source_publication_year":2001,"source_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-slope-working-admission.json","source_pointer":"/width_records/0","current_id":"norwegian-atlantic-slope","canonical_current_id":"norwegian-atlantic-slope","admission_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-slope-working-admission.json","previous_proposed_record_id":"norwegian-atlantic-slope-orvik-2001-regional-width","previous_proposed_source_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-branch-width-scope-audit.json","previous_proposed_source_pointer":"/measurements/0","source_report_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-slope-working-admission.json","canonical_transfer_eligible":true,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"width_rank_eligible":false,"independent_new_observation":false,"geographic_current_edges":null,"physical_current_envelope_admitted":false,"historical_release_admitted":false,"phase_kind":"source_scoped_width_description","phase_label":"Local source-reported width; no seasonal state","time_convention":"Mooring program dates are context, not a dated width series. No annual or seasonal range established.","range_interpretation":"Source-reported regional span; not annual extrema, statistical error or a whole-current width range.","remaining_gates":["Recover paired geographic edges and quantitative error before physical envelope admission.","Acquire comparable repeated dated widths before seasonal or annual geometry."]},{"id":"admitted-width:nwasc:norwegian-atlantic-slope-mork-2010-surface-scale","name":"Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current","status":"working_scoped_source_report_admitted_not_historical_release","source_current_label":"NwASC","measurement_type":"published_ADT_surface_branch_scale","width_metric":"author_reported_surface_branch_scale","approximate_width_km":50,"width_range_km":null,"range_kind":null,"is_confidence_interval":false,"geographic_scope":"Svinoy section, eastern slope branch in surface-velocity description. The source 500 m isobath locates the branch core; it is not a width layer.","layer":"Altimetry-derived absolute geostrophic surface velocity; not the independent 100 m current-meter validation layer.","boundary_rule":"Approximate prose scale associated with Fig. 2; no numerical cutoff or width-edge coordinates extracted. Fig. 2 displays three-month moving averages.","observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"section_geometry":null,"whole_current_representative":false,"rank_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/6/901/2010/","source_citation":"Mork, K. A. and Skagseth, O. (2010), A quantitative description of the Norwegian Atlantic Current by combining altimetry and hydrography, Ocean Science 6, 901-911, doi:10.5194/os-6-901-2010.","source_locator":"Section 3, printed p.904, first paragraph (approximately 50 km); Fig. 2 caption p.903; Sections 2.1-2.2 pp.902-903 and 4.1.1 p.906.","source_access":"Original eleven-page PDF acquired; methods/results/discussion and Figures 2-3 visually inspected. No raw ADT field or width boundaries digitized.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","sampling_context":{"ADT_context_months":{"start":"1992-10","end":"2009-07"},"ADT_context_is_exact_width_observation_interval":false,"surface_grid_resolution_km_at_section_approx":17,"figure_2_moving_average_months":3,"width_is_temporal_mean_or_mean_of_widths":false,"core_bathymetry_m_approx":500,"bathymetry_is_width_layer":false,"validation_instrument_depth_m":100,"validation_depth_is_width_layer":false},"temporal_interpretation":"Regional scale described from a smoothed surface-velocity field. Not an instantaneous width, width of the long-term mean, mean of widths, or numerical seasonal series.","unit":"km","full_width_inference_eligible":false,"source_publication_year":2010,"source_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-slope-working-admission.json","source_pointer":"/width_records/1","current_id":"norwegian-atlantic-slope","canonical_current_id":"norwegian-atlantic-slope","admission_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-slope-working-admission.json","previous_proposed_record_id":"norwegian-atlantic-slope-mork-2010-surface-scale","previous_proposed_source_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-branch-width-scope-audit.json","previous_proposed_source_pointer":"/measurements/2","source_report_file":"research/norwegian-atlantic-slope-working-admission.json","canonical_transfer_eligible":true,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"width_rank_eligible":false,"independent_new_observation":false,"geographic_current_edges":null,"physical_current_envelope_admitted":false,"historical_release_admitted":false,"phase_kind":"source_scoped_width_description","phase_label":"Local source-reported width; no seasonal state","time_convention":"Regional scale described from a smoothed surface-velocity field. Not an instantaneous width, width of the long-term mean, mean of widths, or numerical seasonal series.","range_interpretation":"Source-reported regional span; not annual extrema, statistical error or a whole-current width range.","remaining_gates":["Recover paired geographic edges and quantitative error before physical envelope admission.","Acquire comparable repeated dated widths before seasonal or annual geometry."]},{"name":"Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current","status":"working_scoped_source_report_admitted_not_historical_release","section_geometry":null,"source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/16/685/2020/os-16-685-2020.pdf","source_citation":"Fer, I., Bosse, A., and Dugstad, J. (2020), Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current along the Lofoten Escarpment, Ocean Sci., 16, 685–701, doi:10.5194/os-16-685-2020.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-14","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_hydrographic_section_width","extraction_method":"Transcribed published numerical widths after original-page visual review; no field or edge-coordinate digitization.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"observed_period":null,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"remaining_gates":["Recover paired geographic edges and quantitative error before physical envelope admission.","Acquire comparable repeated dated widths before seasonal or annual geometry."],"id":"admitted-width:nwasc:norwegian-fer-2020-gimsoy-relative-geostrophic-span","source_feature_name":"Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current","phase_kind":"campaign_relative_geostrophic_section_span","phase_label":"Gimsøy four-occupation relative-geostrophic span","measurement_type":"published_campaign_relative_geostrophic_span","width_metric":"relative_geostrophic_transport_density_twenty_percent_span","approximate_width_km":null,"width_range_km":[25,30],"range_kind":"author_reported_characteristic_section_span","range_interpretation":"Author-reported characteristic width span from the four-occupation analysis. No midpoint, per-date widths, confidence bounds or annual extrema.","geographic_scope":"Gimsøy hydrographic section near the Lofoten Escarpment; source-defined Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current, not Norwegian Coastal Current.","section_orientation":"Source hydrographic section across the continental slope; no reconstructed geographic edge coordinates.","layer":"Depth-integrated relative geostrophic current. Exact vertical integration limits for the width paragraph are unspecified; nearby mooring/transport layers are not assigned to width.","time_convention":"Four Gimsøy occupations: 2016-07-30, 2016-11-19, 2017-03-08, 2017-06-07. Source reports one characteristic range, not a width value for each date.","support_dates":["2016-07-30","2016-11-19","2017-03-08","2017-06-07"],"boundary_rule":"Lateral depth-integrated relative geostrophic current reduced to 20% of its maximum; geostrophic reference is surface pressure.","source_locator":"Section 2.2, printed p688/PDF p4; Section 5, printed p692/PDF p8, right-column Gimsøy paragraph.","source_quality_note":"Width integration bounds and numerical width uncertainty unspecified. Effective 20.1 km mooring integration width and assumed 4 km error are different quantities. Slope-current identity admitted separately from the ambiguous Norwegian Current; physical edge geometry remains unresolved.","orig