t al. (2002), section 2, Data and fitting.","locator":"172 sections June 1985-December 2000, ten nominal longitude lines; ADCP mapping and annual-harmonic/SOI fitting.","role":"Sampling and transformation context; does not date the editorial route."}],"candidate_file":"research/pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"0df217ce291f5e8d4804a2fa25f86a2bb8a6fdd5101f00abe2401583ec00df01","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["CAMR","PEQD","PNEC"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_A_3","remaining_gates":["Review editor-selected 110 W/95 W latitudes and interpolating continuity against compatible velocity fields.","Extract depth and month-specific axes before length or width seasonal ranges.","Keep weak or absent surface flow near 110 W separate from subsurface eastward flow; no annual continuous path inferred.","Resolve western inflow and coastal redistribution separately from this truncated studied reach."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent","name":"Pacific North Subsurface Countercurrent","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared northern Tsuchiya Jet studied reach from the 155 W mean-section core to the 110 W mean-section core. Western formation and basin continuation east of 110 W are excluded. The section gates truncate a larger current; interpolating bends are editor-selected, not a measured continuous centerline or particle path.","route_extent_kind":"155 W to 110 W northern Tsuchiya reach","approximate_reference_path_km":5000,"scenario_range_km":[4900,5100],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml","source_locator":"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: north SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 N/220 m and 110 W 4.5 N/130 m. Transport integration latitude limits and 700-dbar reference are separately defined; they are not route width or a uniform axis layer.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml","citation":"Johnson et al. (2002), Direct measurements of upper ocean currents and water properties across the tropical Pacific during the 1990s.","locator":"Section 3.1: northern subsurface countercurrent/Tsuchiya name; 140 W around 4 N/200 m; eastward shoaling and mean/synoptic differences.","role":"Later naming and layer context; not an additional dated or uniform-depth route."}],"candidate_file":"research/pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"0afb68c180bb6a8528173974c6a88641f1f0a22ddc1db5683ee1f95c68760c33","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["PEQD","PNEC"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_A_3","remaining_gates":["Review interpolation against compatible northern Tsuchiya Jet velocity fields; selected section gates are not origins or terminations.","Resolve western formation and eastward turning/merging separately from this studied reach.","Extract month/depth-resolved axes before annual length or width ranges.","Keep NEUC at 130 E and the southern Tsuchiya branches as distinct identities; no transported-volume-to-length or integration-band-to-width conversion."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent","name":"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared historical southern mean-core studied reach from 155 W 3.5 S to 110 W 5.5 S. These gates truncate the larger southern subsurface flow. Western formation, secondary-jet geometry and eastern continuation are excluded. This is one study-defined connection, not an aggregate centerline or sum of primary and secondary branches.","route_extent_kind":"155 W to 110 W historical southern mean-core reach","approximate_reference_path_km":5000,"scenario_range_km":[4900,5100],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml","source_locator":"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: south SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 S/250 m and 110 W 5.5 S/160 m. Latitude integration bands are not widths. Rowe et al. (2000), introduction and section 3e/Fig. 10 caption, distinguish primary and secondary southern jets.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://floats.pmel.noaa.gov/sites/default/files/atoms/files/gcj_1y.pdf","citation":"Rowe, Firing and Johnson (2000), Pacific Equatorial Subsurface Countercurrent Velocity, Transport, and Potential Vorticity, JPO 30, 1172-1187.","locator":"Introduction pp. 1172-1174; data methods pp. 1174-1176; section 3e/Fig. 10 caption p. 1183.","role":"Primary/secondary naming and unresolved splitting/independent origin; front scale is not whole-current width. No route digitized from figures.","license_note":"PDF states AMS copyright; no open license inferred; figures and data not packaged."}],"candidate_file":"research/pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"bb9b13844a2eb7b52c2a25689a900c3f161841acf13a90240b4a7767df57eed1","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["PEQD","PNEC"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_A_4","remaining_gates":["Review correspondence of historical mean-core sections to later primary/secondary labels; no branch aggregation inferred.","R