-system length.","route_extent_kind":"Canary offshore return-flow corridor","approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"scenario_range_km":[1500,1800],"scenario_count":54,"source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/971/2018/","source_locator":"Section 1 Introduction, first paragraph: distinguishes approximately 35-20 N named-current region from wider Canary Current System; bifurcation away from Africa near Cape Blanc (21 N) toward the North Equatorial Current.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/2059/2026/","citation":"Ibrahim and Sun (2026), A multidecadal sea level rise and its hiatus in the tropical Atlantic margin off northwest Africa, Ocean Science 22, 2059-2081, doi:10.5194/os-22-2059-2026.","locator":"Section 4 opening paragraphs: source-region convergence around 35 N and upper-layer context.","role":"Northern geographic naming-gate context; no model axis digitized."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC019487","citation":"Perez-Hernandez et al. (2023), The Seasonal Cycle of the Eastern Boundary Currents of the North Atlantic Subtropical Gyre, JGR Oceans 128, e2022JC019487.","locator":"Abstract and sections 1-2: regional seasonal migration and distinct Lanzarote Passage flow; Table 1 and prose disagree about fall cruise month.","role":"Seasonal continuity caveat; no 2015 observed axis, section width, transport or annual extrema reconstructed."}],"candidate_file":"research/canary-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"b5a8dad9c074d00432e07cb45640469551f1686d3b96e31a4356d0861c7c4309","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/canary-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["CNRY"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_3","remaining_gates":["Review northern feed-region and Cape Blanc naming gates before length admission.","Validate offshore corridor and island clearance using finer coastline, bathymetry and suitable velocity fields.","Resolve source-specific seasonal path and Lanzarote Passage conventions before animated geometry or width extraction.","Canonical admission and publication review; no current footprint or annual extremes inferred."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":{"overlapping_candidate_ids":["north-brazil-reference-path-candidate","labrador-reference-path-candidate","agulhas-reference-path-candidate","somali-winter-reference-path-candidate","alaska-reference-path-candidate","kuroshio-extension-reference-path-candidate","portugal-reference-path-candidate"],"envelope_position_bounds":[14,21],"interpretation":"Conservative positions within retained rounded route envelopes, treating choices independently; touching envelopes overlap. Not a statistical rank interval or a uniform whole-current comparison."}},{"id":"south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"south-indian","name":"South Indian Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared 70 E to 90 E eastern-name-convention regional reach. The west gate follows the later convention reserving South Indian Ocean Current for flow beyond the Agulhas Return Current near 70 E; the east gate is the approximate recirculation/splitting region described in historical hydrography. These are selected regional gates, not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.","route_extent_kind":"eastern regional reach","approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"scenario_range_km":[1600,1800],"scenario_count":27,"source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455","source_locator":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997), section 3.2 / journal p. 5523 and Figure 7 caption: 90 E recirculation/split and upper-1000 m flow schematic. Later Grand et al. (2015), regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113: SIOC name beyond 70 E. Near-40 S context from Stramma (1992) publisher abstract; drawn latitudes are editorial.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/abstract/journals/phoc/22/4/1520-0485_1992_022_0421_tsioc_2_0_co_2.xml","citation":"Stramma (1992), The South Indian Ocean Current, JPO 22, 421–430.","locator":"Publisher abstract only: near-40 S STF context and eastern separation beyond 100 E.","supports":"Broad earlier current name and approximate frontal geography; no source centerline digitized."},{"url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924796301000410","citation":"Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001), The Agulhas Return Current, Journal of Marine Systems 30, 115–138.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct publisher retrieval returned 403.","supports":"Proposed ARC termination near 66–70 E and SIOC name farther east; source convention, not fixed physical junction."},{"url":"https://science.whoi.edu/users/mcgillic/cruises/TN376/cruiseshare/Morton%20lab/Relevant%20Papers/Grand%20et%20al.%20-%202015%20-%20The%20impact%20of%20circulation%20and%20dust%20deposition%20in%20controlling%20the%20distributions%20of%20dissolved%20Fe%20and%20Al%20in%20the%20south.pdf","citation":"Grand et al. (2015), The impact of circulation and dust deposition in controlling the distributions of dissolved Fe and Al in the south Indian subtropical gyre, Marine Chemistry 176, 110–125.","locator":"Regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113 / PDF page 4.","supports":"SIOC name beyond 70 E; near-90 E recirculation and dispersed eastern flow."}],"candidate_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"5ffe93eddca3a110dedfc3a0d2dfb589504d60422e24729e0820629b4a94eafe","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/south-indian-eastern-reach-