on from the named current; eastern filament context cites earlier work.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://pureadmin.uhi.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/14119479/2020GL088350.pdf","citation":"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt, Claus and Hahn (2020), Fluctuations of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Associated Changes in Oxygen Transports, GRL 47, e2020GL088350, doi:10.1029/2020GL088350.","locator":"Introduction and sections 2–4, pp. 1–4: central 5 N, 23 W observations and 65–270 m definition; data intervals and fixed-box/inferred-transport distinctions.","role":"Central observational context; weak seasonal cycle and episodic intraseasonal events do not establish seasonal geometry."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014760","citation":"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt and Duteil (2019), Interannual Variability of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Its Impact on Oxygen, JGR Oceans 124, 2348–2373, doi:10.1029/2018JC014760.","locator":"Introduction, sections 2.1 and 2.3: 23 W ship sections; model half-width and observational integration boundaries.","role":"Distinguishes chosen transport integration widths and model-domain longitude span from diagnosed current dimensions."}],"candidate_file":"research/atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"386796f3f152bc36828c6f3a1c88f262f9f8a054c1f2f3465839dae252af34ca","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["WTRA"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_3","remaining_gates":["Diagnose a compatible subsurface axis before asserting continuity across the separate section neighborhoods.","Resolve source recirculation, eastern filaments and termination before whole-current length.","Review historical two-degree latitude width with boundary and month-date precision support; no whole width or seasonal range inferred.","Keep mooring transport variability distinct from seasonal length/width geometry."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"davidson","name":"Davidson Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_approximate_reference_routes","scope":"California-Oregon winter coastal reference corridor between OSW gates at 35 N and 46 N. These are bookkeeping gates, not source-published current endpoints. Excludes conditional Vancouver Island penetration and the deeper California Undercurrent. No full-system length or width footprint.","route_extent_kind":"historical winter regional corridor","approximate_reference_path_km":1300,"scenario_range_km":[1200,1400],"scenario_count":54,"source_url":"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf","source_locator":"Appendix II section II.1, printed II-1 to II-2 / PDF pages 12-13: northward seasonal surface strip along California and Oregon from October to March; Vancouver Island penetration is conditional.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"ac2db281859e27e8903fb224f3fdde35b36f010ab111240e2a2c78e3c5a26609","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["CCAL","OCAL"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_A_2","remaining_gates":["Review source observational basis, current boundaries and historical applicability.","Validate coastal vertices and named-flow gates using bathymetry and suitable winter velocity fields.","No conditional Vancouver Island extension or deeper California Undercurrent merger.","Canonical admission and publication review; this is an editorial regional route length."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null