s or termination.","route_extent_kind":"eastern Solomon Islands reference reach","approximate_reference_path_km":900,"scenario_range_km":[800,1000],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html","source_locator":"Melet et al. (2010) coauthor abstract proposes SICU east of Solomon Islands; original model axis not acquired. Ganachaud et al. (2017), Figures 2 and 7 and pages 11-12/17, supply island geography and local observational context, not a continuous SICU axis.","supporting_sources":[{"label":"Ganachaud et al. (2017), Solomon Sea cruises","url":"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.221","locator":"Figures 2 and 7; pages 5-7, 11-12 and 17","access":"Original NOAA-hosted PDF acquired and institutional SHA256 matched; CC BY 4.0 printed page 27; selected pages and figures inspected."}],"candidate_file":"research/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"64c8f36d57216f978f94ed81debd6f4d8d95b74c985ee613870c3a41d2c7942d","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["AUSE","WARM"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_G_4","remaining_gates":["Acquire and visually review the original 2010 model Figure 4 before digitizing a model axis.","Review finer coastline and bathymetry, source velocity fields and the density-dependent flow before identifying an actual current core.","Resolve complete entrance/exit gates and connectivity to NICU separately; no connector across Solomon Strait is drawn.","No whole-current width, annual range, dated footprint or NASA surface identification inferred."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"east-adriatic","name":"East Adriatic Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scien