errupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.","route_extent_kind":"66 N–Cape Farewell studied reach","approximate_reference_path_km":800,"scenario_range_km":[800,900],"scenario_count":81,"source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","supporting_sources":[],"candidate_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"606edd4cfe959e577c65a0a089b607006ed878823af280f113bba682da6af680","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["SARC"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_B_1","remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and shelf bathymetry before claiming an inner-shelf current axis.","Resolve northern identification and the 63 N merger before any whole-current extent.","Do not replace the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey description with this shorter editorial reach.","Retain the Cape Farewell 30 km threshold width as a local section; no width buffer or annual footprint inferred."],"parent_current_id":null,"parent_scope_note":null,"ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"monsoon","name":"Monsoon Current","status":"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed","comparison_group":"osw_studied_reach_routes","scope":"Declared 77–83 E Sri Lanka regional summer reach, oriented eastward. Gates and connecting vertices are selected by OSW; neither gate is a physical whole-current endpoint. Excludes Arabian S