etry supplied.","role":"Naming reference only; does not define this coastal reach or certify Northern Current segment boundaries."},{"url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/689/2018/","citation":"Berta et al. (2018), Wind-induced variability in the Northern Current (northwestern Mediterranean Sea) as depicted by a multi-platform observing system, Ocean Science 14, 689–710, doi:10.5194/os-14-689-2018.","locator":"Introduction: Liguro-Provencal-Catalan / Northern Current formed in Ligurian Sea and recognizable through Catalan Sea.","role":"Broader parent geography; whole-parent length and regional width summaries are not transferred to this segment."}],"candidate_file":"research/ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","candidate_sha256":"097cef899d328b72f4069125e1f30d3d5663a9502ca500d74d0ccbeb318a0bba","generator_sha256":"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240","figure":"figures/ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg","nominal_atlas_state_crossings":["MEDI"],"recommended_nasa_tile_id":"level2_C_2","remaining_gates":["Resolve the geographic Ligurian naming convention before whole-segment endpoint admission.","Review source sampling/layer and coastal path with finer bathymetry or compatible current data.","Keep overlapping Northern Current and Ligurian segment lengths separate; do not sum them.","Review local 20 km Menton–Nice profile-band extraction, mixed surface support and remaining Imperia coast-distance limit; no paired whole-current width inferred."],"parent_current_id":"northern-mediterranean","parent_scope_note":"The ledger treats Ligurian Current as a Northern Current segment. This studied reach overlaps the broader current geography; do not add its length to the parent or count it as an independent parallel flow.","ordering_sensitivity":null},{"id":"redsox-southern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate","current_id":"red-sea-saline-overflow","name":"Red Sea saline overflow - southern plume reference reach","status":"ed