m":"OGC:CRS84","positional_uncertainty":"not quantified; no observed current core or path","source_id":"source:4dc5fc618c26565f"}],"state_evidence":[],"connections":[],"scope_notes":[{"current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","label":"Source-described passage network and exit observations","audit_file":"research/indonesian-throughflow-network-scope-audit.json","summary":"Twelve conceptual nodes and fourteen selected passage connections; three 2004–2006 exit transport means and eight published mooring sites. No whole-system length, geographic graph edges or transfer of integration widths to physical current width.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","source_locator":"Introduction paragraphs 3–4, Tables 1–2 and section 2.2","observed_period":{"start_year":2004,"end_year":2006,"precision":"year"}},{"current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","label":"Measurement object scope: passage network","audit_file":"research/current-measurement-scopes/indonesian-throughflow.json","summary":"Measure each passage with explicit depth, period and boundary rules. Channel and transport-integration spans are not current-width boundaries.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","source_locator":"Existing cited current ledger entry and explicit component links; retained source-scope audit research/indonesian-throughflow-network-scope-audit.json","observed_period":null,"measurement_scope_assessment":true,"related_current_ids":[],"related_proposed_current_ids":[]}],"evidence_links":[{"label":"Open passage network card","url":"query.html?q=%7B%22collection%22%3A%22flow_networks%22%2C%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22filters%22%3A%5B%7B%22field%22%3A%22id%22%2C%22op%22%3A%22eq%22%2C%22value%22%3A%22flow-network%3Aindonesian-throughflow%22%7D%5D%7D&inspect=flow-network%3Aindonesian-throughflow"},{"label":"Map exit transport mooring sites","url":"query.html?q=%7B%22collection%22%3A%22passage_samples%22%2C%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22filters%22%3A%5B%7B%22field%22%3A%22network_id%22%2C%22op%22%3A%22eq%22%2C%22value%22%3A%22flow-network%3Aindonesian-throughflow%22%7D%5D%7D"}],"object_url":"object.html?id=current%3Aindonesian-throughflow","route_url":null,"season_url":"seasons.html?current=indonesian-throughflow","scope_audits":[{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","as_of":"2026-10-04","status":"source_supported_conceptual_network_not_scientific_taxonomy_admission","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","source_access":"Publisher Introduction paragraphs 3–8, Tables 1–2 and section 2.2 read; no figure, field or transport time-series digitized.","source_locator":"Introduction paragraphs 3–4; Tables 1–2; section 2.2.","network_file":"research/indonesian-throughflow-network-input.json","summary":"Selected western/eastern inflow and three main exit pathways represented as twelve conceptual nodes and fourteen connections. Three exit transport means retain 2004–2006 support, processing-choice intervals and eight published first-deployment mooring positions. No geographic network edges, full system length, current width, annual extrema or instantaneous one-way-flow claim.","observed_period":{"start_year":2004,"end_year":2006,"precision":"year"},"source_time_caution":"Abstract mentions January 2003; Table 1 explicitly reports 2004–2006 averages. Individual mooring deployment dates differ, including an August 2003 Ombai deployment. Preserve these distinctions.","integration_width_caution":"35/35/160 km are transport-integration widths, not current widths. Ombai geographic width is discussed as 37 km in paragraph 8, while transport calculations use 35 km. Neither provides a uniform current footprint.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"rank_eligible":false,"canonical_taxonomy_admitted":false,"remaining_gates":["Assess full pas