r relation to coarse masked OSW display polygons."}],"state_evidence":[],"connections":[],"scope_notes":[{"current_id":"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent","label":"Northern Tsuchiya mean cores and integration limits","audit_file":"research/pacific-nscc-reach-layer-section-scope-audit.json","summary":"155 W to 110 W is an editorial northern Tsuchiya studied reach. Local mean cores shoal from 220 m to 130 m; no uniform axis depth inferred. Transport integration latitude limits are not width. Historical compilation dates do not date the route, and the 130 E NEUC identity is kept separate. A separate Rowe et al. general 2-degree meridional width summary is now retained as approximately 220 km; the two jet records share one source claim, not independent observations or annual extrema.","source_url":"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml","source_locator":"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: north SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 N/220 m and 110 W 4.5 N/130 m. Transport integration latitude limits and 700-dbar reference are separately defined; they are not route width or a uniform axis layer.","observed_period":null}],"evidence_links":[],"object_url":"object.html?id=current%3Apacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent","route_url":"reference-routes.html#pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate","season_url":"seasons.html?current=pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent","dashboard_search":"Pacific North Subsurface Countercurrent Equatorial North Pacific","width_ids":["pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent-rowe-2000-general-angular-width"],"measurement_ids":[],"route_ids":["pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"source_ids":["source:b038491b0e5a3967","source:df8a86f107aba236"],"state_codes":[],"published_length_km":null,"width_sample_ids":[],"route_decision_ids":["route-decision:pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent"],"current_section_ids":[],"velocity_sample_ids":[]},{"id":"current:pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Pacific South Equatorial Countercurrent","type":"named_current","identity_level":"current","source_kind":"seasonally varying eastward countercurrent","setting":"equatorial","time_behavior":"seasonal","basin":"Tropical South Pacific","capabilities":{"observed_velocity":0,"radius_evidence":0,"reported_length":0,"reference_route":0,"scoped_width":1,"geometry":0,"time_samples":0,"source_connectivity":0,"scope_notes":2,"dated_diagnostics":0,"flow_network":0,"passage_transport":0,"width_samples":0},"recorded_claims":56,"nasa_links":1,"fingerprint":"9df275d8ad33da61ba16e7116f8e767d7371b474c8a2a2e282c6e46c23e1bc20","series":[],"section_fingerprints":{"identity":"0a7c9e3aeadc47415d4d10a028f9175f4ae733f8e295ba3a97a4b47de019c4a4","sources":"c01001fb290345298b71eb8eb2cf5e545d46f5360685b9be789d23ec6f4d6b4b","claims":"a2260e85e85cdaacd05696a2bbc881fb6f1e636ebc87bed5300f637bf643449c","measurements":"48898dff5dc1c51f0d87ec135947e45563dfef5209883cd906076bda24075e23","routes_geometry":"74aeb995dc693bc0f23130b0cba8251d723d2686090deea7764749eca886698f","media":"68658cd0ec2f73124154cc258620ecc3b963fde1f88b1db76b5ddb15420c2128","time_evidence":"8d86da8229951992c802d517eaeaeeb84a4b5f1a3e916ecd7944f448135387bd"},"latest_observation_date":null,"claim_review_counts":{"not_individually_reviewed":56},"linked_source_count":3,"map_features":[{"geometry":{"coordinates":[165,-9],"type":"Point"},"role":"editorial_locator","note":"Representative point inside Argo-observed boreal-spring 150°E–170°W, 5–13°S envelope; not a path endpoint.","geometry_id":"geometry:0099","coordinate_reference_system":"OGC:CRS84","positional_uncertainty":"not quantified; no observed current core or path","source_id":"source:4dc5fc618c26565f"}],"state_evidence":[],"connections":[],"scope_notes":[{"current_id":"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Argo seasonal envelope and dateline scope","audit_file":"research/pacific-secc-argo-seasonal-extent-scope-audit.json","summary":"Source preview reports a spring envelope from 150 E to 170 W and an autumn extension to 140 W. These dateline-crossing spans are not traced current lengths. Spring latitude limits are not paired current edges; full methods, averaging years and calendar months remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2025JC023053?af=R","source_locator":"Publisher abstract, Plain Language Summary and Data Availability Statement.","observed_period":null},{"current_id":"pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"WOA01 mean flow and seasonal anomaly separation","audit_file":"research/pacific-secc-woa01-anomaly-scope-audit.json","summary":"Full 2004 paper distinguishes surface and 0-200 m WOA01 geostrophy relative to 1500 dbar, modeled Sverdrup flow, and band-passed seasonal anomaly sections at 170 E. Anomaly zero contours and averaging windows cannot define current widths or endpoints. Numerical compatible flow fields remain needed.","source_url":"https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/oceanography/bo/CQ04.pdf","source_locator":"Figures 1, 2 and 8; paragraphs 2-3, 20 and 26.","observed_period":null}],"evidence_links":[],"object_url":"object.html?id=current%3Apacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","route_url":null,"season_url":"seasons.html?current=pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent","dashboard_search":"Pacific South Equatorial Countercurrent Tropical South Pacific","width_ids":["pacific-secc-rotschi-1972-170e-width-range"],"measurement_ids":[],"route_ids":[],"source_ids":["source:b038491b0e5a3967","source:cb7e6dd38745baf6"],"state_codes":[],"published_length_km":null,"width_sample_ids":[],"route_decision_ids":["route-decision:pacific-south-equatorial-countercurrent"],"current_section_ids":[],"velocity_sample_ids":[]},{"id":"current:pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent","label":"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent","type":"named_current","identity_level":"current","source_kind":"eastward subsurface jets south of the Equatorial Undercurrent","setting":"equatorial","time_behavior":"persis