gy using 1993-2018 drifter context. Not a dated trajectory or complete annual route series.","layer":"Surface drifter climatology with GDP drogue support near 15 m and wind-slip-corrected undrogued observations; not a uniform fixed-depth current axis or full vertical extent. OSCAR upper-layer and deeper current diagnostics remain separate.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483","source_locator":"Sections 2.1-2.2: drifter support, 1993-2018 selection, fitted seasonal fields and December-March winter. Section 3 seasonal discussion after Figures 5-6: eastward SECC reaches about 90 E before recirculating into SEC; Figure 13 caption.","entity_id":"current:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent — December-March eastward surface reach","status":"editorial_seasonal_route_associations_not_canonical","seasonal_inventory_file":"research/ocean-current-seasonal-route-frames.json","seasonal_inventory_sha256":"5e2bbbcf1aa91253b8ca7d114765364640f62390533af513f205764af63e4422","coordinates_lon_lat":[[50,-4],[60,-4],[70,-4],[80,-4],[90,-4]],"comparability":{"current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"reason":"One December-March surface studied reach with editorial gates and vertices. Other seasonal axes and paired-edge widths are unavailable. Its 4400-4500 km drawing envelope is not annual length variation."}}],"geometry_frames":[{"id":"query-frame:current:gulf-stream-system:2025-01-15:fixed-seed-geostrophic","entity_id":"current:gulf-stream-system","series_id":"query-series:current:gulf-stream-system:0","label":"Gulf Stream System — 2025-01-15 frozen-field diagnostic","status":"research_only_not_canonical_or_ranked","timeline_file":"research/ocean-current-dated-timeline-2025.json","timeline_sha256":"3f157216b7bb4ef345921b083dd693eb754ea22459112a1da6a13806b4a7dfb9","layer":"Altimetry