 extrema.","geographic_scope":"Cape Hatteras offshore fixed TR-038 baseline; three non-synoptic crossings in1967. Not the whole Gulf Stream or Gulf Stream System.","section_orientation":"Width along a baseline bearing135 degrees true; transport velocity is the component normal to that baseline. Recorded flow directions vary; no exact flow-normal projection applied.","layer":"Transport per unit width integrated from surface to local bottom, with variable bathymetry. No fixed-depth width layer or surface-only speed boundary.","time_convention":"Three complete crossings1,3,4:30June–5July,11–15July,16–18July1967. Campaign26June–18July is separate. Multi-day occupations, not simultaneous snapshots or continuous monthly/seasonal means; source clock timezone unspecified.","boundary_rule":"Authors smooth transport-per-unit-width measurements and extend their curves to zero. No negative inshore transport was observed; inshore edges are extrapolated. Two complete crossings have offshore negative values, one offshore edge is also extended to zero.","source_url":"https://www2.whoi.edu/staff/prichardson/wp-content/uploads/sites/75/2018/11/Richardson-Knauss-1971-dsr.pdf","source_citation":"Richardson, P. L. and Knauss, J. A. (1971), Gulf Stream and Western Boundary Undercurrent observations at Cape Hatteras, Deep-Sea Research18,1089–1109, doi:10.1016/0011-7471(71)90095-7.","source_locator":"Methods printed1091/PDF3; Fig2 printed1093/PDF5; zero-edge construction printed1094–1095/PDF6–7; Table2 printed1105/PDF17; mean135 km printed1107/PDF19.","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_transport_float_campaign_statistics","extraction_method":"Transcribed explicit author widths and mean; matched complete occupations using Figure2 and Table2. No curve digitization, geographic endpoints or width error inferred.","phase_label":"1967 three complete crossings · zero-transport spans","phase_kind":"campaign_width_statistics","observed_period":{"start":"1967-06-30","end":"1967-07-18"},"source_quality_note":"Inshore zero boundaries are author extrapolations, not observed sign reversals. Multi-day sampling and changing flow direction limit synoptic/flow-normal interpretation. Baseline135 degrees differs from mean135 km.","remaining_gates":["Recover geographic boundary coordinates and the original transport observations.","Quantify section-orientation, interpolation and sampling uncertainty.","Independent scientific admission before whole-current dimensions or annual variability."],"original_regional_context":{"description_kind":"gulf_stream_transport_float_complete_crossing_statistics","complete_crossing_occupations":[{"id":"gulf-stream-1967-crossing-1","crossing_number":1,"observed_period":{"start":"1967-06-30","end":"1967-07-05"},"width_km":145,"transport_sv":58,"source_clock_timezone":null,"is_synoptic_snapshot":false},{"id":"gulf-stream-1967-crossing-3","crossing_number":3,"observed_period":{"start":"1967-07-11","end":"1967-07-15"},"width_km":140,"transport_sv":67,"source_clock_timezone":null,"is_synoptic_snapshot":false},{"id":"gulf-stream-1967-crossing-4","crossing_number":4,"observed_period":{"start":"1967-07-16","end":"1967-07-18"},"width_km":120,"transport_sv":64,"source_clock_timezone":null,"is_synoptic_snapshot":false}],"partial_crossing_without_width":2,"reported_mean_width_km":135,"mean_is_independent_occupation":false,"campaign_context_period":{"start":"1967-06-26","end":"1967-07-18"},"baseline_bearing_degrees_true":135,"baseline_bearing_is_width":false,"width_is_exact_flow_normal_projection":false,"author_boundary_extrapolation_present":true,"inshore_negative_transport_observed":false,"offshore_negative_transport_observed_complete_crossing_count":2,"all_paired_edges_observed_sign_reversals":false,"source_curve_or_coordinates_digitized":false,"occupation_range_is_uncertainty_or_annual_extrema":false,"display_aria_label":"Gulf Stream off Cape Hatteras: three author zero-transport section widths145,140,120 km in1967; reported mean135 km and finite sample span120–145 km. Author extrapolation is retained; no annual extrema or geographic edges.","display_caption":"Mean135 km; three complete1967 crossings span120–145 km. Published zero-transport curve edges include extrapolation.","display_method_note":"Surface-to-local-bottom transport, fixed135-degree-true baseline; multi-day occupations and varying direction. Mean is not a fourth occupation; finite spread is not uncertainty or annual variability.","comparison_figure":"figures/gulf-stream-published-width-definitions.svg","comparison_figure_label":"Compare published Gulf Stream width definitions"}},{"current_id":"gulf-stream","name":"Gulf Stream","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","section_geometry":null,"whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"calendar_months":null,"fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"uncertainty_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-14","id":"gulf-stream-lozier-1995-climatological-isopycnal-span","measurement_type":"published_climatological_isopycnal_contour_span","width_metric":"mean_isopycnal_pressure_contour_separation","width_metric_label":"Historical climatology: sigma-theta26.50 pressure contours","approximate_width_km":300,"width_range_km":null,"range_interpretation":"One approximate author-reported mean contour span. Meander envelope500 km, smoothing scale100 km and factor-of-two comparison are separate context; no150 km inferred observation or combined135–300 km range.","geographic_scope":"Gulf Stream near70 W on the mean sigma-theta26.50 surface; not the entire current or its larger system.","section_orientation":"Author contour separation near70 W; exact geographic endpoints and flow-normal orientation not extracted.","layer":"Potential-density-anomaly surface sigma-theta26.50. Width between100 and400 dbar pressure contours on that surface; these are not fixed100–400 m depth bounds.","time_convention":"Historical isopycnal climatology from the NODC archive available as of April1990. Basin-wide observations span1904–1990; exact local averaging dates and seasonal weights are unresolved. Publication1995 is not an observation date.","boundary_rule":"Author estimates mean width from the separation of100 and400 dbar contours on the sigma-theta26.50 isopycnal near70 W, rather than paired velocity edges.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/science/po/people/rcurry/pdf_files/Lozier_etal.PiO1995.pdf","source_citation":"Lozier, M. S., Owens, W. B. and Curry, R. G. (1995), The climatology of the North Atlantic, Progress in Oceanography36,1–44, doi:10.1016/0079-6611(95)00013-5.","source_locator":"Abstract printed1/PDF1; section2 printed3/PDF3; section5.1 printed14–17/PDF14–17; Figure7 printed15/PDF15; width and meandering discussion printed17/PDF17.","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_historical_isopycnal_climatology","extraction_method":"Transcribed explicit about300 km contour span after original-page review. No contour digitization, depth conversion, exact local period or inferred instantaneous width.","phase_label":"Historical climatology · near70 W contour span","phase_kind":"climatological_isopycnal_span","observed_period":null,"source_quality_note":"Mean pressure contours on an isopycnal differ from instantaneous transport or half-speed boundaries. Local period and width error unresolved; pressure levels are not fixed depths.","remaining_gates":["Recover exact local contribution dates, contour geography and orientation.","Assess smoothing, averaging and meandering effects independently.","Independent scientific admission before geographic footprint or physical annual dimensions."],"original_regional_context":{"description_kind":"gulf_stream_historical_mean_isopycnal_contour_span","isopycnal_label":"sigma-theta26.50","pressure_contours_dbar":[100,400],"pre