certainty is not reported. Transport uncertainty is a separate quantity. Separate cruises and layers are not an annual range.","geographic_scope":"Gulf Stream 36∘ N; source longitude limits -71.7:-69.1 degrees east. Section track may deviate from nominal latitude near boundaries. Endpoint latitudes remain unextracted.","section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Nominally zonal hydrographic track; boundary/platform stations may deviate to cross the main flow. Exact boundary track orientation unresolved.","layer":"Publisher neutral-density layer indices 1:6; reported depth extent 0 to 891 m. Density surfaces are not a uniform fixed-depth slice.","time_convention":"74AB20050501: section sampled 2005-05-03 to 2005-06-12; inverse-model group 2000–2009. Cruise snapshot, not a decade mean or seasonal composite.","boundary_rule":"Section 2.3: station pairs selected by consistent slope of eastward accumulated horizontal mass transport; vertical extent by the same integrated flow direction. No fixed speed cutoff or instantaneous velocity envelope inferred.","boundary_sides":"source_selected_station_limits","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/","source_citation":"Caínzos et al. (2023), Consistent picture of the horizontal circulation of the Atlantic Ocean over 3 decades, Ocean Science 19, 1009–1045, doi:10.5194/os-19-1009-2023.","source_locator":"Table 2, Worksheet 1, row 59, columns A–F; Table 1 row 13; Sections 2.1–2.3.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-07","source_evidence_kind":"published_inverse_model_hydrographic_cruise_snapshot","extraction_method":"Publisher XLSX cells retained and distance transcribed directly; explicit section/cruise join. No map or longitude-to-distance conversion.","whole_current_representative":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"is_confidence_interval":false,"phase_kind":"inverse_hydrographic_section_span","phase_l