 reference flow, exact evaluation depth and geographic edges unresolved; no annual range.","display_caption":"About100 km · prestorm geostrophic core at fixed0.4 m/s cutoff.","display_method_note":"Thermal-wind density analysis relative to750 m or bottom. Upper300 m core context is not a uniform width layer. Source e-folding wording is not adopted; no width-error or seasonal interval.","comparison_figure":"figures/loop-uhlhorn-2008-core-width.svg","comparison_figure_label":"Inspect the Loop Current core width definition"}}}},{"id":"diagnostic:south-pacific-dated-band-constraint","label":"South Pacific March 1990 relative-geostrophic band constraint","entity_id":"current:south-pacific","current_id":"south-pacific","status":"reviewed_original_source_constraint_for_editorial_integration","rank_eligible":false,"source_file":"research/south-pacific-stramma-1995-width-constraint-scope-audit.json","source_file_sha256":"5d86b40f0c1029535542b843dd5b1451d6111b1ddcd16e82a6a02d438d1c7578","source_json":"{\n  \"schema\": \"osw.south-pacific-band-constraint-source-audit.v1\",\n  \"status\": \"reviewed_original_source_constraint_for_editorial_integration\",\n  \"current_id\": \"south-pacific\",\n  \"source_document_file\": \"research/source-data/stramma-south-pacific-1995/journal-article.pdf\",\n  \"source_document_sha256\": \"9b471dbdeb5a010bda7411c40dcaa939fb5c55d1559c3a89c8281ca10c2efd28\",\n  \"source_pages\": 15,\n  \"acquisition_file\": \"research/source-data/stramma-south-pacific-1995/acquisition.json\",\n  \"acquisition_sha256\": \"f526c22e6c9818083ce9aa6c4a0840c7731e5610a86bcb03e204897e3f7f301d\",\n  \"protocol_file\": \"plans/south-pacific-stramma-width-constraint-protocol-v1.md\",\n  \"protocol_sha256\": \"4bb82a91eccdd46a8f94bd9f83168dd6102105a6de642fc91e1d2f1c67635dfe\",\n  \"figure_file\": \"figures/south-pacific-stramma-1990-band-constraint.svg\",\n  \"figure_sha256\": \"7b6e2df10289091c3f4072f6eb00caf46dc3fe49a59608e0f5de5b6b8e14fe45\",\n  \"source_review\": {\n    \"method\": \"Visual original page review; OCR for discovery only\",\n    \"publication_pages\": [\n      79,\n      82,\n      83,\n      84,\n      89\n    ],\n    \"source_curves_digitized\": false,\n    \"source_pdf_is_image_scan\": true\n  },\n  \"measurement\": {\n    \"id\": \"south-pacific-stramma-1990-03-relative-band-constraint\",\n    \"current_id\": \"south-pacific\",\n    \"name\": \"South Pacific Current\",\n    \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\n    \"measurement_type\": \"published_month_relative_geostrophic_band_width_constraint\",\n    \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_current_width\",\n    \"approximate_width_km\": null,\n    \"width_range_km\": null,\n    \"range_kind\": \"author_reported_dated_less_than_width_constraint\",\n    \"range_interpretation\": \"Reported enhanced eastward band less than200 km in one historical section. Representative width, lower bound, confidence limits, whole-current envelope and annual range remain unknown.\",\n    \"geographic_scope\": \"Western South Pacific near Chatham Rise; Baldrige section d at nominal170 W in March1990. Front station table gives170.6 W; exact width edges unresolved.\",\n    \"section_geometry\": null,\n    \"section_orientation\": \"Nominal meridional hydrographic section; no diagnosed flow-normal axis or paired width endpoints.\",\n    \"layer\": \"Enhanced eastward relative-geostrophic band in Figure3 upper1000 m context. Surface-intensified flow; exact width-evaluation depth unknown. No uniform vertical width slab.\",\n    \"time_convention\": \"March1990, late austral summer, from Table1(d) and Figure3 caption. Exact occupation days and annual coverage unavailable.\",\n    \"boundary_rule\": \"Author reports band less than200 km wide. No numeric edge cutoff or geographic edge pair supplied; peak/sampled velocities are context only.\",\n    \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0485(1995)025<0077:TSPC>2.0.CO;2\",\n    \"source_citation\": \"Stramma, L., R.G. Peterson and M. Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, Journal of Physical Oceanography25,77-91.\",\n    \"source_locator\": \"Original p82 right column; Table1(d) p79, Table2(d) p83 and Figure3/caption p84. Rejected illustrative100 km assumption: p89.\",\n    \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-17\",\n    \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_original_scan_reviewed_relative_geostrophic_band_constraint\",\n    \"extraction_method\": \"Source qualifier and context transcribed after visual review of original pages. No source curve or edge digitization.\",\n    \"whole_current_representative\": false,\n    \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\n    \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\n    \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\n    \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\n    \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\n    \"phase_label\": \"Baldrige enhanced eastward band / March 1990\",\n    \"phase_kind\": \"month_dated_width_constraint\",\n    \"observed_period\": null,\n    \"calendar_months\": null,\n    \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\n    \"uncertainty_km\": null,\n    \"source_quality_note\": \"Original15-page scan retained unchanged and ignored. Full field curves, edge coordinates and width uncertainty have not been digitized or inferred. Frontal bracket differs from velocity width.\",\n    \"remaining_gates\": [\n      \"Recover author boundary definition and exact evaluation depth before paired physical edges.\",\n      \"Acquire compatible repeated sections before seasonal widths or annual extrema.\",\n      \"Independent scientific admission.\"\n    ],\n    \"original_regional_context\": {\n      \"source_quote\": \"less than 200 km wide\",\n      \"source_section\": \"d / RV Baldrige\",\n      \"observed_month\": \"1990-03\",\n      \"nominal_section_longitude_degrees_east\": -170,\n      \"front_table_longitude_degrees_east\": -170.6,\n      \"front_station_latitudes_degrees_north\": [\n        -43.5,\n        -42.5\n      ],\n      \"front_bracket_is_width_edges\": false,\n      \"relative_geostrophic_reference\": {\n        \"potential_density_symbol\": \"sigma_2\",\n        \"value_kg_m3\": 36.75,\n        \"source_reference_depth_range_m\": [\n          1800,\n          1840\n        ],\n        \"reference_is_width_layer\": false\n      },\n      \"source_velocity_context\": {\n        \"surface_peak_cm_s\": 7,\n        \"near_500m_cm_s\": 4,\n        \"velocities_are_width_cutoffs\": false\n      },\n      \"field_plot_depth_context_m\": [\n        0,\n        1000\n      ],\n      \"field_plot_context_is_uniform_width_layer\": false,\n      \"illustrative_transport_width_km\": 100,\n      \"illustrative_transport_width_is_observation\": false,\n      \"axis_to_ACC_separation_km\": {\n        \"operator\": \"gt\",\n        \"value\": 500,\n        \"is_current_width\": false\n      },\n      \"display_method_note\": \"One reported less-than band constraint; representative width, lower bound, numerical uncertainty, mapped edges and annual extrema remain unknown. March 1990 dates the observation; 1995 is publication. The 100 km transport assumption and greater-than-500 km separation from ACC flow are distinct contextual values.\",\n      \"display_aria_label\": \"South Pacific Current: the authors report an enhanced eastward band less than 200 km wide near nominal 170 W in March 1990. Relative geostrophic reference sigma2=36.75 kg/m3 at 1800-1840 m. Representative width, exact days, lower bound and error unknown. No 200 km point, zero-to-200 interval, geographic width band or annual range.\",\n      \"display_caption\": \"March 1990 / Baldrige section d near nominal 170 W. Source-reported constraint for an enhanced eastward relative-geostrophic band; representative width and paired edges unknown.\"\n    },\n    \"reported_width_constraint\": {\n      \"kind\": \"author_reported_dated_less_than\",\n      \"operator\": \"lt\",\n      \"reference_scale_km\": 200,\n      \"source_notation\": \"<200 km\",\n      \"i