al_peak_search_complete":false,"supported_local_core_followup":false,"status":"incomplete_peak_search_or_missing_profile"},{"fraction":0.4,"velocity_offset_m_s":0.04,"conditional_unverified_profiles_included":true,"span_km":null,"left_edge":null,"right_edge":null,"unavailable_profile_ids":["rsx2-034-hr"],"global_peak_search_complete":false,"supported_local_core_followup":false,"status":"incomplete_peak_search_or_missing_profile"},{"fraction":0.6,"velocity_offset_m_s":0,"conditional_unverified_profiles_included":true,"span_km":null,"left_edge":null,"right_edge":null,"unavailable_profile_ids":["rsx2-034-hr"],"global_peak_search_complete":false,"supported_local_core_followup":false,"status":"incomplete_peak_search_or_missing_profile"},{"fraction":0.6,"velocity_offset_m_s":-0.04,"conditional_unverified_profiles_included":true,"span_km":null,"left_edge":null,"right_edge":null,"unavailable_profile_ids":["rsx2-034-hr"],"global_peak_search_complete":false,"supported_local_core_followup":false,"status":"incomplete_peak_search_or_missing_profile"},{"fraction":0.6,"velocity_offset_m_s":0.04,"conditional_unverified_profiles_included":true,"span_km":null,"left_edge":null,"right_edge":null,"unavailable_profile_ids":["rsx2-034-hr"],"global_peak_search_complete":false,"supported_local_core_followup":false,"status":"incomplete_peak_search_or_missing_profile"}]}],"current_association_verified":false,"width_rank_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"new_width_record_admitted":false,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null},"research_evidence":{"current_id":"red-sea-saline-overflow","label":"Red Sea saline overflow","diagnostic_id":"diagnostic:current-research:red-sea-saline-overflow","title":"Observed sections: independent local span estimates","finding":"Winter casts 7, 8 and 9 support a roughly 6 km half-peak southward-component section span in the layer 40–80 m above bottom. This local-core follow-up is separate from the unresolved primary calculation at 20–60 m. It does not establish a whole-current or flow-normal width. A separate source-declared cross-channel section on 22–23 February supports a southern local span of about 5.0 km at 20–60 m above bottom and 5.5 km at 40–80 m. Its northern branch remains unresolved. The 23 August repeat gives a northern component candidate near 3.1 km, but it fails the unchanged saline-water screen. No same-branch winter–summer width difference is supported.","facts":[{"label":"Earlier northern section span","value":"About 6 km · 40–80 m above bottom"},{"label":"Earlier primary 20–60 m result","value":"Unresolved"},{"label":"Whole-current width","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Annual width range","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Independent southern section","value":"About 5.0 km · 20–60 m above bottom"},{"label":"Independent northern section","value":"Unresolved"},{"label":"Summer northern component candidate","value":"About 3.1 km · saline screen fails"}],"notes":["The local span covers only 1.67 native station spacings. The core vector is about 15.7° from the section normal; no cosine correction or precise physical-boundary claim is made.","The 40% threshold remains unresolved. Finite velocity, boundary and layer scenarios are not combined into a confidence interval.","A conditional value near 7.3 km in the 20–60 m layer uses excluded winter cast 10 and does not replace the primary unknown. Summer lacks comparable usable layer/reference support; it is not zero width or proof of an absent current.","Original headers, reviewed metadata and filename-only cast joins remain distinct. The declaration-history note records prior incidental exposure to three cast 10 rows; no fully blinded preregistration is claimed.","The new section preserves all 30 fixed cases: ten southern component spans and twenty unresolved outcomes. The deeper-layer 40% threshold extends to 12.6 km; this is finite scenario sensitivity, not an annual margin or confidence bound. The 10–50 m layer lacks complete support. Casts 61/63 remain excluded; cast 74 has no CTD companion. No tidal removal or whole-current width admission.","The summer peak has about 37.41 source psu, below the unchanged 38 psu screen; the −0.04 m/s offset also puts it below the speed floor. This does not prove the named outflow is absent. Cast22 remains excluded for unverified bad-upcast treatment. All30 summer cases and all6 same-branch comparisons are retained. Two dates cannot establish an annual range or seasonal climatology; different branches are never combined to fill missing comparisons."],"next_evidence":"Resolve rejected-component treatment and water-mass/flow association; obtain paired usable boundaries and repeated observations before physical-width or seasonal-range admission.","figure_file":"figures/redsox-lower-nc-section-diagnostic.svg","figure_alt":"Winter and summer layer velocity and salinity. A roughly 6 km secondary-layer local span is distinguished from unknown primary and summer outcomes.","source_file":"research/redsox-lower-nc-dated-section-diagnostic.json","source_pointer":"","source_links":[{"label":"Inspect all layers and null scenarios","document":"research/redsox-lower-nc-dated-section-diagnostic.json","pointer":""},{"label":"Inspect direct-current source inventory","document":"research/redsox-ladcp-source-inventory.json","pointer":""},{"label":"Inspect hydrography and filename joins","document":"research/redsox-ctd-companion-inventory.json","pointer":""},{"label":"Inspect reviewed source metadata","document":"research/redsox-cruise-log-metadata-reconciliation.json","pointer":""},{"label":"Inspect declaration-history qualification","document":"research/source-data/redsox-lower-nc-2001/declaration-history-note.json","pointer":""},{"label":"All 30 independent section cases","document":"research/redsox-winter-section3-component-spans.json","pointer":"/layers"},{"label":"Source section selection and original hashes","document":"research/redsox-section3-source-selection.json","pointer":""},{"label":"Declared independent section rules","document":"research/redsox-section3-source-selection.json","pointer":"/protocol_file"},{"label":"Independent section figure provenance","document":"research/redsox-winter-section3-figure.json","pointer":""},{"label":"Summer section: all 30 declared cases","document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.json","pointer":"/summer_layers"},{"label":"Six same-branch dated comparisons","document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.json","pointer":"/comparisons"},{"label":"Matched source station positions","document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.json","pointer":"/station_correspondence"},{"label":"Summer section selection and rules","document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-source-selection.json","pointer":""},{"label":"Repeat-survey figure provenance","document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-figure.json","pointer":""}],"original_url":"https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/archive/accession/0146147","table":{"caption":"Two non-synoptic 2001 surveys; outcomes are section diagnostics, not annual current widths.","headers":["Survey","Layer above bottom","Supported local half-peak span"],"rows":[["18 Feb 2001","20–60 m","Unresolved"],["18 Feb 2001","10–50 m","Unresolved"],["18 Feb 2001","40–80 m","About 6 km · follow-up"],["24 Aug 2001","20–60 m","Unresolved"],["24 Aug 2001","10–50 m","Unresolved"],["24 Aug 2001","40–80 m","Unresolved"]]},"additional_figures":[{"file":"figures/redsox-winter-section3-component-spans.svg","label":"Independent source-declared winter section","alt":"Twelve source-ordered casts on 22–23 February 2001, paired layer velocities, hydrography and all fixed southern sensitivities. Primary local span about 5.0 km, deeper-layer half-peak 5.5 km; northern and shallow-layer results unresolved. Physical whole-current width and annual range unknown."},{"file":"figures/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.svg","label":"Two dated surveys: velocity and salinity comparison","alt":"February and August 2001 paired layer components and salinity from twelve repeated station neighborhoods. Winter southern spans are about5.0/5.5km; summer northern candidate3.1km fails the unchanged saline screen and is not a verified width. Southern summer is quality-blocked; northern winter is incomplete. No same-branch width difference or annual range is supported."}],"additional_tables":[{"caption":"Independent Section 3, 22–23 February 2001. Local half-peak section spans; not whole-current widths.","headers":["Layer above bottom","Southern local span","Northern local span"],"rows":[["20–60 m","About 5.0 km","Unresolved"],["10–50 m","Unresolved","Unresolved"],["40–80 m","About 5.5 km","Unresolved"]]},{"caption":"22–23 February versus23 August2001, Section3. Different branches are separate; component candidates are not physical widths. All six same-branch dated differences remain unresolved.","headers":["Layer above bottom","Winter south","Summer south","Winter north","Summer north","Same-branch difference"],"rows":[["20–60 m","About 5.0 km","Unresolved","Unresolved","About 3.1 km · saline screen fails","Unresolved"],["10–50 m","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved"],["40–80 m","About 5.5 km","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved"]]}],"query_links":[{"label":"Query all dated section measurements","query":{"collection":"current_section_measurements","filters":[{"field":"current_id","op":"eq","value":"red-sea-saline-overflow"}],"limit":100}}],"kind":"current_research_evidence","rank_eligible":false,"new_width_record_admitted":false,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"geometry_role":"research_evidence_no_current_axis_or_physical_width_geometry","figure_sha256":"f56167fb865d8a8eca58b00cbc8a496a7414097dabcbf2487f56c490d356c8b7"}},{"id":"diagnostic:current-research:norwegian-coastal","label":"Norwegian Coastal Current research evidence","entity_id":"current:norwegian-coastal","current_id":"norwegian-coastal","status":"reviewed